                <pb facs="1022" n="908" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg908"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.001 Montero, Juan/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-21T16:00:00-05:00">August 21, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:54 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>96. My telegram number 95, August 18, 6 p.m. The Senate has refused to accept
                    resignation of Montero. Nevertheless as a candidate <pb facs="1023" n="909"
                        xml:id="pg909"/> for the presidency he has insisted upon turning over the
                    power temporarily to the Minister of the Interior, Manuel Trucco, who becomes
                    Vice President until after the elections.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
